Suppose $ee = p \/ q$ with $p, q in NN$ and $q > 1$, using $2 < ee < 3$. Then
$ q! dot ee = q! + (q!)/(1!) + ... + (q!)/(q!) + sum_(j=q+1)^oo (q!)/(j!) = N + x $
with $N in NN$ and $x = sum_(j=1)^oo (q!)/((q+j)!)$. Since $(q!)/((q+j)!) <= (1)/((q+1)^j)$, we get $0 < x <= (1)/(q+1) + (1)/(q+1)^2 + ... <= (1)/(q) < 1$. So $0 < x < 1$ while $N + x = q! ee$ is a natural number, which is impossible. Hence $ee$ is irrational.
